    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "28. Open Your Own Treasure House"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a803dcbc7f712287e5729a85cd9f16da"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:text """Daiju visited the master Baso in China. Baso asked: 'What do you seek?'

'Enlightenment,' replied Daiju.

'You have your own treasure house. Why do you search outside?' Baso asked.

Daiju inquired : 'Where is my treasure house?'

Baso answered: 'What you me asking me is your treasure house.'

Daiju was enlightened! Ever after he urged his friends:

'Open your own treasure house and use those treasures.'"""^^xsd:string .

