    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "70. The Most Valuable Thing in the World"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c2c46fbc86ba92c8e1a4e80c31a6f226"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:text """Sozan, a Chinese Zen master, was asked by a student: 'What is the most valuable thing in the world?'

The master replied: The head of a dead cat.'

'Why is the head of a dead cat the most valuable thing in the world?' inquired the student.

Sozan replied: 'Because no one can name its price.'"""^^xsd:string .

