        ex:node_4_93f9d1d9_2fb5_44aa_a733_3324445f03ca_555,
        ex:node_4_93f9d1d9_2fb5_44aa_a733_3324445f03ca_803,
        ex:node_4_93f9d1d9_2fb5_44aa_a733_3324445f03ca_883 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "THE GATELESS GATE"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "10. Seizei Alone and Poor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2c7863a6216f4921c998c9dbaa6f6610"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:text """A monk named Seizei asked of Sozan: "Seizei is alone and poor. Will you give him support?"

Sozan asked: "Seizei?"

Seizei responded: "Yes, sir."

Sozan said: "You have Zen, the best wine in China, and already have finished three cups, and still you are saying that they did not even wet your lips."

Mumon's comment: Seizei overplayed his hand. Why was it so? Because Sozan had eyes and knew with whom to deal. Even so, I want to ask: At what point did Seizei drink wine?

The poorest man in China, The bravest man in China, He barely sustains himself, Yet wishes to rival the wealthiest."""^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_93f9d1d9_2fb5_44aa_a733_3324445f03ca_884 a neo:Document ;
